    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d719">

                <pb facs="0953" n="841" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg841"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 417.00/246</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jefferson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-21T15:00:00-05:45">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 21, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have been urged by the High Commission and many creditors who have accepted
                    awards of the Public Credit Commission to request the Department to authorize as
                    early as possible the High Commission to begin payments of awards.</p>
                <pb facs="0954" n="842" xml:id="pg842"/>
                <p>The High Commission cabled Nicaraguan Chargé d’Affaires Enriquez with reference
                    to this matter.</p>
                <p>It is my opinion that payments should begin as soon as possible as it will
                    relieve the economic situation here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
